      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havre%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was originally called 'Bullhook Bottoms' before settlers chose the name Havre, inspired by Le Havre, France.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havre%2C_Montana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Earl Clack Memorial Museum showcases Havre's history, archaeology, and paleontology, reflecting the town's deep roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visithavremt.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Wahkpa Chug’n Buffalo Jump nearby lets visitors learn about ancient Native American bison hunting practices.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visithavremt.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
